# Release build output. cmd/verso/dist/index.html is a committed placeholder —
# //go:embed all:dist needs the directory to exist before the client has ever
# been built — but the hashed assets `make build` copies over it are artifacts.
cmd/verso/dist/assets/

# Not published: every entry in this lockfile resolves through a private
# corporate registry, so committing it would leak that hostname and tenant
# namespace into a public repo. Nothing in the build reads it — the Dockerfile
# copies a prebuilt web/dist — so `npm install` from web/package.json is enough
# to develop. To publish it properly, re-resolve it against the public registry
# first:  cd web && npm install --package-lock-only --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
web/package-lock.json
